{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793357866,"nonce":"gVLVkLNXXiHWxuHywDOGq/Sz5Zk=","title":"Release needs a breaking-version decision and migration notes against published 0.5.1","message":"The requested release API review compared published blinc_core, blinc_gpu, blinc_layout and blinc_app 0.5.1 archives and docs.rs Rustdoc JSON against local a8d5aaef76f627f670ebe0c1e04b0eeb8a9d2ad1. The subsequent test-directory-only commit 3fad1735b41204c7f080f75b34784f2db1571c1b does not change these APIs. This is a targeted default-feature rendering/API review, not a formal all-crate/all-feature/all-target semver-checks pass; published JSON is Linux, current JSON macOS, so target-only differences were excluded from confirmed findings.\n\nRecommendation: coordinate the next release as 0.6.0, rather than 0.5.2, unless the published API breaks are deliberately reverted. Existing public struct field changes, enum variants and GPU repr(C) changes independently require the pre-1.0 minor bump. Workspace still declares 0.5.1; current crates.io metadata reports that version already published for 24 of the curated 25 release crates. blinc_css is new/unpublished. Versions/internal dependency pins and consumer migration notes remain release work; no versions were changed and nothing was published.\n\nConfirmed core changes: TextureData no longer supports the old public rgba field or raw struct literals; use TextureData::new(bytes, width, height), and with_bytes for optional retained CPU data. MeshData vertices/indices now use Arc\u003cVec\u003c_\u003e\u003e and gains morph data, Material gains fields, ClipShape::RoundedRect gains corner_shape. use_signal now requires Clone. New DrawContext hooks have default bodies, so the reviewed hooks do not introduce mandatory implementation methods.\n\nConfirmed GPU changes: LayerCommand has additional exhaustive variants and Sample gains paint; DynamicImage, PrimitiveBatch and command entry raw literals gain fields. render_mesh_data replaces light_dir/light_intensity with a DirectionalLight slice; blit_tight_texture_to_target adds rotate_z_rad (0.0 for no rotation). RendererConfig gains pipeline_cache_path. Public repr(C) field declarations give these old/current sizes in bytes: GpuPrimitive 368/544, GpuImageInstance 192/208, SdfVertexInstance 128/144, GlassUniforms 16/32, MaskImageUniforms 16/32. PathVertex stays 120 but repurposes padding for clip_shape; LayerCompositeUniforms stays 112 but replaces padding with rotation fields. GpuGlyph stays 96 and GpuGlassPrimitive stays 144. Custom uploads/shaders must follow current field offsets and semantics, not just total size. Sizes/offsets were checked using standalone Rust representations generated from the published/current compiler JSON, not external-device ABI tests.\n\nConfirmed layout/app changes: PendingSubtreeRebuild replaces needs_layout with RebuildKind and adds epoch/tree_scope; existing public event/render/config records gain fields. Button::new/with_content signatures change. WindowedContext::use_scroll_ref takes no argument; explicit keys use use_scroll_ref_keyed. WindowedContext::use_state now returns reactive State\u003cT\u003e; FSM consumers use use_fsm/use_fsm_keyed (the old use_state_for alias is deprecated). The old inherent use_effect is absent. Built-in ImageRenderInfo opacity is now neutral 1.0 because node opacity is owned by RenderProps.\n\nImportant false-positive exclusions: GroupGlass, native cross-stream Capture and PartialPropertyUpdate are new since published 0.5.1. GroupGlass.nested is a public CPU metadata field specifying whether to sample prior paint within the enclosing glass isolation; ordinary first-level literals use false. Adding it changes local development callers, but is not independently a published-0.5.1 API break or GPU/shared ABI change. GroupGlass review covers this meaning, literal construction, first-level behavior and cache fingerprinting. The broader version/MSRV/GPU findings are separate release concerns. Historical blinc_layout::css_parser, element_style, units and calc paths are preserved by public reexports; canonical source-module movement is not a removal of those paths. This review does not authorize owner-gated shared ClipPath/fill-rule or DSL work.\n\nEvidence: /private/tmp/blinc-api-baseline/ archives + JSON, /private/tmp/blinc-api-current/ JSON, /private/tmp/blinc_api_compare.py, /private/tmp/blinc-release-api-candidates.log and per-crate candidates. Candidate lists include moves/target differences and must not be treated as an unfiltered break report. /private/tmp/blinc-api-layout-probe.{rs,log}; /private/tmp/blinc-release-registry-cohort.json. Scoped cargo rustdoc completed for these four libraries, with CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2. scripts/publish_crates.py --plan resolves the curated 25-crate graph but does not verify packages. Rust 1.88 checks pass for these four libraries; declared MSRV/CI mismatch is a separate blocker. Actual package verification, release version/pins/migration notes, hosted/device/browser checks and the unsupported rendering combinations in parent e0a7502 remain open.\n\nReferences: https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/semver.html and https://docs.rs/about/rustdoc-json. No source/tracker push or publication.","files":null}]}